{title: Redeemed, How I Love to Proclaim It}
{artist: Fanny Crosby / William J. Kirkpatrick}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Three (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing, 1950), # 126)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Redeemed, how I love to proclaim it!
[G]Re[D]deemed by the blood of the [G]Lamb;
[G]Redeemed through His infinite mercy,
[G]His [D7]child and forever I [G]am.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Re[C]deemed, re[G]deemed,
[G]Re[D]deemed by the blood of the [G]Lamb;
[G]Re[C]deemed, re[G]deemed,
[G]His [D7]child and forever I [G]am.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Redeemed, and so happy in Jesus,
[G]No [D]language my rapture can [G]tell;
[G]I know that the light of His presence
[G]With [D7]me doth continually [G]dwell.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I think of my blessèd Redeemer,
[G]I [D]think of Him all the day [G]long:
[G]I sing, for I cannot be silent;
[G]His [D7]love is the theme of my [G]song.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]I know I shall see in His beauty
[G]The [D]King in whose law I de[G]light;
[G]Who lovingly guardeth my footsteps,
[G]And [D7]giveth me songs in the [G]night.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]I know there’s a crown that is waiting,
[G]In [D]yonder bright mansion for [G]me,
[G]And soon, with the spirits made perfect,
[G]At [D7]home with the Lord I shall [G]be.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
